  "plain": "A US pilot named Fred Clawson says there were missions between the CIA, the Air Force and Varginha, a town in Brazil where, by other accounts on the show, a craft crashed in 1996 and a living being was captured, and that these missions were later scrubbed from the record. Michels introduces him as now saying this on record. Clawson tells it himself and adds detail: he says that \"in order to secure a cargo plane, a specific protocol must be adhered to,\" and that the paper trail leads back to Scott Air Force Base. If he is right, the United States played a hidden part in the Varginha events."
